Pasal 21
( 1) Pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 20 ayat (2) huruf a bertujuan untuk:
a. membantu korban mengenali permasalahannya dan menemukan cara-cara yang efektif untuk mengatasinya sendiri;
b. memberdayakan korban untuk menentukan masa depannya; c. memberikan dukungan moral bagi korban dalam menghadapi proses hukum yang dijalaninya; dan
d. membuat korban merasa diterima di lingkungan masyarakat. (2) Pelayanan konseling dilakukan oleh petugas rehabilitasi sosial yang responsive gender, terdiri atas:
a. konselor yang telah memiliki sertifikat;
b. psikolog; dan
c. psikiater.
(3) Pelayanan konseling dilakukan di tempat yang menjamin rasa aman, nyaman dan kerahasiaan informasi dari korban. (4) Tahapan pelayanan konseling meliputi:
a. konseling awal;
b. konseling lanjutan;
c. pembahasan kasus; dan
d. kunjungan ke lokasi.

translated_text:
Article 21
(1) Social rehabilitation services as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (2) letter a aim to:
a. assist victims in recognizing their problems and finding effective ways to overcome them independently;
b. empower victims to determine their future; c. provide moral support for victims in facing the legal processes they undergo; and
d. make victims feel accepted in the community environment. (2) Counseling services are conducted by social rehabilitation officers who are gender responsive, consisting of:
a. counselors who have obtained certificates;
b. psychologists; and
c. psychiatrists.
(3) Counseling services are conducted in places that guarantee a sense of security, comfort and confidentiality of information from victims. (4) Stages of counseling services include:
a. initial counseling;
b. follow-up counseling;
c. case discussion; and
d. site visits.
